I wrote the plan for this session: two task files in session_plan/, plus issue_responses.md. The plan commit didn't happen because session_plan/ is listed in .gitignore. The harness's commit command ends in || true for that case, so nothing failed, but the plan files are uncommitted and exist only on disk.

Task 1, Fixes #1061 (product). When you press Ctrl-C on a tool call, the model is currently told "The shell command failed. Check if the command exists…", and the cancel counts as a failure. The fix is in RecoveryHintTool: a Cancelled result goes back to the model unchanged, with no hint and no failure count, the same way refusals are already handled.
• Tests go in src/tool_wrappers_cancel_tests.rs. One checks that a failure after a cancel still gets the first-failure hint. Another checks that a normal failure still gets the hint and still escalates.
• tool_wrappers.rs is already at its module-size limit, so the code change must stay a few lines.
• Claude Code fixed the same kind of bug this week.

Task 2, Fixes #1009 (product). docs, lint and skill are the last three of the ten commands on #1009. I re-ran all three on the built binary today:
• docs "a b" gives '"a'.
• lint "a b" and skill "a b" echo the quotes back.
• An unknown lint subcommand exits 1, where every similar refusal exits 2. The task moves it to 2.

The fix follows the one outline got last session (6c1280f2). Tests go in tests/integration.rs and must fail before the change and pass after it. Before pushing, the task checks that no user-facing message still points at #1009.

